WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.387
As teams mature, usually with a Center of Excellence behind them,

00:00:04.397 --> 00:00:08.370
they close that gap by putting every solution under source control.

00:00:09.293 --> 00:00:11.043
The maker still builds in dev.

00:00:11.513 --> 00:00:16.943
But now the PAC CLI exports the solution, and unpacks the zip into plain source files.

00:00:17.901 --> 00:00:22.571
Every app, table and flow becomes readable text, committed to a Git repository.

00:00:23.581 --> 00:00:28.031
Each change has a history, an author, and a pull request that someone reviews.

00:00:29.069 --> 00:00:32.619
When a change is merged, an automated pipeline takes over.

00:00:33.069 --> 00:00:37.519
It packs the source back into a managed solution, a fresh build every time.

00:00:39.738 --> 00:00:43.788
That same build is deployed to test, and once it's approved, to production.

00:00:44.298 --> 00:00:46.328
Nobody imports anything by hand.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.900
Git is now the source of truth.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:53.940
If dev breaks, you rebuild it from the repo, or roll back to any earlier version.
